{
 "description": "Shared recipient path vectors. 'relative' entries run against the recipient core's Confined and Python's checked_relative (expect), and against deployment.target and ProjectPaths.output (expect unless 'legacy' names an intentional difference). 'roots' run against the core's Checked and Python's checked_path. A synthetic root holds a junction named 'linked' to a folder outside it. Tokens: {root}, {root_posix}, {drive}, {x255}, {x256}, {emoji127}, {emoji128}. Python and the core always match 'expect'; a row may name an intentional core 'difference' only with the exact 'powershell' result.",
 "differences": {
  "legacy-normalizes": {
   "kind": "intentional",
   "reason": "deployment.target and ProjectPaths.output receive paths through pathlib, which collapses '.', empty components and trailing separators before the check. They resolve to the normalised target inside the root, so nothing escapes. checked_relative is the reference for the recipient core's stricter Confined rule; Python production targets keep the normalising rule so existing deployment receipts stay readable."
  }
 },
